# SECTION 14 — GLOBAL FLASHCARD ACCURACY & VALIDATION

This rule applies to all Card creation and import methods.

## Manual Cards

- Validate Front and Back.
- Do not allow empty fields.
- Do not modify user-written text silently.

## Image Cards

- Validate OCR text.
- Preserve source information where possible.
- Identify low-confidence text.
- Do not silently invent missing words.

## PDF Cards

- Validate against extracted source text.
- Preserve page references.
- Identify unsupported or uncertain content.
- Do not claim complete accuracy.

## JSON / CSV Cards

- Validate file structure.
- Validate required fields.
- Identify empty fields and duplicates.
- Do not silently rewrite imported facts.

## UNIVERSAL RULES

- Never invent answers.
- Never silently change source facts.
- Never alter dates or numerical values without user approval.
- Never mark uncertain content as verified.
- Detect duplicates.
- Detect mismatched Questions and Answers wherever possible.
- Detect unsupported information wherever source material is available.
- Detect incomplete content.
- Allow editing before import.
- Allow deleting before import.
- Invalid Cards must not be silently imported.
- Inform the user about skipped Cards and the reason.
- User must control final Card selection and saving.

Accuracy is more important than the quantity of generated Cards.

100% error-free automatic generation cannot be guaranteed. The app must never falsely claim that a Card is error-free simply because automated validation passed.

For Image and PDF generation, source verification and human review must remain available.

For JSON and CSV, validate structure and data integrity without falsely claiming factual verification of unsourced content.

